## 7. On model size

Current: **261,402 parameters.**

```
item_embed     (100, 64)     6,400
entity_embed   (40, 64)      2,560
tile_embed     (16, 16)        256
embed_proj     (256, 592)   151,552     <- 58% of the network
fc1            (256, 108)    27,648
fc2            (256, 256)    65,536
actor          (25, 256)      6,400
critic         (1, 256)         256
```

Raising it is reasonable **when the signal for it appears**, and that signal
is: the agent plateaus while still improving on its training rungs. That is
what running out of capacity looks like.

What is happening now is the opposite — maximum entropy while ignoring a
signal it is being handed. Adding width to that produces a more fluent
wanderer. Size is not the binding constraint today.

The grid world is likewise the right call, not a compromise. Thousands of
episodes have to run and be watched on a modest laptop; 3D would cost a
hundred times the compute to teach the same lesson more slowly.

